        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a for-profit public company headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, trading under the ticker LUMN and SEC CIK 0000018926. Its website describes the company as providing a global fiber network with secure networking, edge cloud, and AI-ready infrastructure to connect people, data, and apps. The site calls Lumen the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy and says its fiber footprint reduces latency to support real-time performance.\n\nThe company's site presents AI-ready networking and secure cloud solutions. It highlights customer examples: Arctic Glacier replaced manual operations with built-in automation, the New York Yankees use diverse 100G paths and automatic failover for always-on performance, and American Family Care needed an AI-era network while scaling across 26 states. The site also says Prometheus Hyperscale anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady, and that retail customers use the network for real-time inventory, AI-driven personalization, and DDoS protection.\n\nThe company has 57 legal exposure entries in Louisiana. No litigation cases are listed.",
